# Genuine predefined sizing input producer

This Source-only proposal retains the two actual SimulationControl alpha inputs
needed by the full predefined registry. It is unapplied and unexecuted. It adds
no runtime output, fixture injection, Native answer or alternate registry.

TypedModel.predefined_table_sizing owns an optional first
SimulationControlSizingInput: actual object identity, the two uppercase/default
alpha values, original blank facts and default-applied facts. The owner's
actual_flags() preserves Native GetProjectData's false reset and independent
Alphas(1)==YES / Alphas(2)==YES tests. No object means no getter owner and both
flags false. An object with missing/empty fields has actual IDD No defaults,
kept separately from explicit No. The real registry can consume this pair once
and retain its own allocations and IDs for the subsequent postlude.

The compiler uses its existing ordered object access and single_object helper.
SimulationControl is a genuine unique-object declaration. Only admitted Yes/No
strings are released; malformed types, choices and multiple unique objects use
existing compiler diagnostics and withhold the typed model. These admissions
describe normal input processing, not arbitrary bypassed Native getter state.
The method resets the input owner before parsing and uses existing default
recording rather than a second default mechanism. The existing report parser
calls it once; all five report-family parsing bodies otherwise remain exact.

Native InputProcessor substitutes the schema default for empty/missing alpha
fields, marks them blank and uppercases non-retaincase fields. The pinned IDD
has No defaults for both selected fields. SimulationManager then reads only
the first actual object. This proposal preserves those facts and does not
infer a sizing flag from the presence of Sizing:Zone/System objects or from
whether sizing eventually runs.

The remaining SimulationControl fields, full sizing execution/validation,
GetProjectData side effects and general whole-simulation compatibility remain
separate scope. For example, independent flags preserve the direct assignment
boundary even though later Native validation can reject system sizing without
zone sizing. This partial prerequisite is not counted as full typed support
for the SimulationControl object and does not change object-count accounting.

The five unexecuted tests cover absence, missing/empty defaults and their facts,
case-normalized independent YES inputs, malformed choice/type and duplicate
unique objects. Existing report DTOs and manually supplied Scan observer
records remain structurally unchanged; no observer fixture needs an invented
new SimulationControl input.

Only report_inputs.rs, model.rs and compiler/report_inputs.rs change. Exact
current before archives, all three regenerated diffs and bounded Native/current
Source ranges are pinned. Model field/Default and the parser's single call are
additive. All prior report parsing, tests and typed-count code remain literal.
The registry itself remains immutable in its separately held final02 package.

Root and another author must FULL-review this hold before application. Ordinary
registry/postlude/output-context plumbing remains Base's separate proposal and
must consume this actual producer owner without hardcoded false flags. Genuine
Native registry/report observations and byte comparisons remain required;
there is no registry, report, whole Init or CTF10 PASS claim here. No project
import, compiler, test, formatter, target, binary, scientific output, canonical
edit or Git operation was performed.
